 in an OLRC note at 42 U.S.C. 3121 note)","quote":"Ex. Ord. No. 11493, Nov. 13, 1969, 34 F.R. 18289, which created Council for Rural Affairs to advise President with respect to further development of non-metropolitan areas of country, was revoked by Ex. Ord. No. 12553, Feb. 25, 1986, 51 F.R. 7237.","quote_truncated":false,"system":"usc","where":"USC 42 U.S.C. 3121 note"},"proposal":{"actor":"EO:12553","date":"1986-02-25","mechanism":"revocation","source":{"page_or_item":"42 U.S.C. 3121 note; note 'Executive Order No. 11493' [USLM note id id3ad65ff3-c3e9-11f1-bd73-d95596aaa024]; usc42.xml (sha256 9a2ce8ea01dfa97423fcd8749e7534a64c0ec75df9bf56584b210c0725a66692) in xml_uscAll@119-121.zip","sha256":"c6122974e951003437ece5a998aa7c0b2cdc0f5703dfc78d6135e1fc9e729142","url":"https://uscode.house.gov/download/releasepoints/us/pl/119/121/xml_uscAll@119-121.zip"}},"suggested":false},{"custody_records_in":[],"group":{"actor":"EO:12553","corroborated_by_two_jobs":true,"date":"1986-02-25","jobs":["current-law","later-events","ofr-codification-1989"]},"meta":{"acting_instrument_id":"EO:12553","caution":"1989 OFR editorial codification: the Executive Orders disposition table states the order's status as of 1989-01-20 (OCR table cell, rows paired by position). The date is the acting document's signing date, not its effective date; the order (or parts of it) may have ceased earlier by its own terms. Read the acting instrument","date_basis":["acting order signing_date from OFR catalog (jobs/later-events EDGES.csv)"],"evidence_types":["ofr_codification_1989_table"],"flags":["ocr_table_cell_not_human_verified","ofr_codification_1989_editorial","status_as_of_1989-01-20","whole_end_from_1989_disposition_table"],"from":"ofr-codification-1989@jobs/ofr-codification-1989/output","from_job":"ofr-codification-1989","ids":["OC89-8202f3aebdf2"],"quote":"Revokedby EO 12553","quote_kind":"ocr_table_cell","quote_truncated":false,"status":"CANDIDATE_UNVERIFIED"},"proposal":{"actor":"EO:12553","date":"1986-02-25","mechanism":"revocation","source":{"page_or_item":"OFR Codification 1945-1989 (1989), Executive Orders disposition table, printed page 1073, PDF page 1084","sha256":"6c760d36b1d22350dc22890bbf31afb0a67911c3bc295abd567cc0e706fe2ccd","url":"https://hdl.handle.net/2027/uiug.30112026470077"}},"suggested":false}],"whole_order_end_total":3},"provisional_status":"no","readiness":{"by_step":{"clause_inventory":"confirm","counterevidence":"confirm","ending_or_current_basis":"confirm","opus_media":"n/a","original_text":"confirm","savings_residuals":"agent_judgment","shared_sources":"n/a"},"needs_research":[],"would_satisfy_once_confirmed":["original_text","clause_inventory","ending_or_current_basis","counterevidence"]},"shared_sources":[],"signing_dates_seen":{"fr-originals@jobs/fr-originals/output":"1969-11-13","later-events_catalog":"1969-11-13","stage19_causal_queue":"1969-11-13"},"source_ladder_exhausted_proposed":[],"status":"MACHINE DRAFT - UNVERIFIED; not a claim; see jobs/claim-drafts/AGENT_GUIDE.md"},"claim":{"instrument_id":"EO:11493","later_source_search":[],"operative_clauses":[{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) There is hereby es­\ntablished the Council for Rural Affairs (hereinafter referred to as  \n“the Council”).","original_source":{"page_or_item":"34 FR 18289, PDF pages 5-6; Sec. 1(a)","sha256":"f522d7ceb7cb8dd8a14d4ceaad5eecedb213f066d2dd6b9e5fc36c9b76b4d445","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1969-11-15/pdf/FR-1969-11-15.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11493#sec1(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) The President of the United States shall preside over meetings  \nof the Council. The Vice President shall preside in the absence of the  \nPresident.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"34 FR 18289, PDF pages 5-6; Sec. 1(b)","sha256":"f522d7ceb7cb8dd8a14d4ceaad5eecedb213f066d2dd6b9e5fc36c9b76b4d445","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1969-11-15/pdf/FR-1969-11-15.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11493#sec1(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) The Council shall be composed of the following:\nThe Vice President of the United States\nSecretary of Agriculture\nSecretary of Interior\nSecretary of Commerce\nSecretary of Health, Education and Welfare\nSecretary of Housing and Urban Development\nSecretary of Labor\nChairman of the Council of Economic Advisers  \nDirector of the Bureau of the Budget  \nDirector of the Office of Economic Opportunity\nand such other heads of departments and agencies as the President may  \nfrom time to time direct.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"34 FR 18289, PDF pages 5-6; Sec. 1(c)","sha256":"f522d7ceb7cb8dd8a14d4ceaad5eecedb213f066d2dd6b9e5fc36c9b76b4d445","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1969-11-15/pdf/FR-1969-11-15.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11493#sec1(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"S ec. 2 . Functions of the Council.  The Council shall advise and as­\nsist the President with respect to the further development-of the non­\nmetropolitan areas of the country and shall perform such other duties  \nas the President may from time to time prescribe. In addition to such \nduties, the Council is directed to :","original_source":{"page_or_item":"34 FR 18289, PDF pages 5-6; Sec. 2 (lead-in)","sha256":"f522d7ceb7cb8dd8a14d4ceaad5eecedb213f066d2dd6b9e5fc36c9b76b4d445","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1969-11-15/pdf/FR-1969-11-15.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11493#sec2","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(1) Assist the President in the development of policies for rural  \nareas, which shall include consideration of the affairs of the smaller  \ncities and towns which lie outside the metropolitan areas.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"34 FR 18289, PDF pages 5-6; Sec. 2(1)","sha256":"f522d7ceb7cb8dd8a14d4ceaad5eecedb213f066d2dd6b9e5fc36c9b76b4d445","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1969-11-15/pdf/FR-1969-11-15.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11493#sec2(1)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(2) Secure information on the problems confronting rural America,  \nidentify their causes, and develop means to deal with them by using  \navailable programs or initiating new ones.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"34 FR 18289, PDF pages 5-6; Sec. 2(2)","sha256":"f522d7ceb7cb8dd8a14d4ceaad5eecedb213f066d2dd6b9e5fc36c9b76b4d445","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1969-11-15/pdf/FR-1969-11-15.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11493#sec2(2)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(3) Foster effective use and coordination of Federal programs in  \nthe non-metropolitan areas in order to improve the delivery of public  \nservices to the people.\nFEDERAL REGISTER, VO L 34, NO. 220— SATURDAY, NOVEMBER 15, 1969\n\n=== PDF page 6 of 64 ===\n18290 THE PRESIDENT\n(4) Encourage the fullest cooperation between Federal, State, and  \nlocal governments, with special concern for local initiative and local  \ndecision-making.\n(5) Ensure that in the development of policies and programs con­\ncerning rural affairs, the relationships between urban, suburban, and  \nrural areas are taken into account.\n(6) Encourage the most effective role possible for voluntary orga­\nnizations in dealing with rural problems and their solutions.\n~(T) Encourage an improved geographical distribution of the pop­\nulation of the United States.\n(8) Keep the President advised on progress in meeting: national  \nobjectives.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"34 FR 18289, PDF pages 5-6; Sec. 2(3)","sha256":"f522d7ceb7cb8dd8a14d4ceaad5eecedb213f066d2dd6b9e5fc36c9b76b4d445","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1969-11-15/pdf/FR-1969-11-15.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11493#sec2(3)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"S ec. 3. Administrative arrangements.  In compliance with provisions  \nof applicable law, and as necessary to effectuate the purposes of this  \norder,","original_source":{"page_or_item":"34 FR 18289, PDF pages 5-6; Sec. 3 (lead-in)","sha256":"f522d7ceb7cb8dd8a14d4ceaad5eecedb213f066d2dd6b9e5fc36c9b76b4d445","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1969-11-15/pdf/FR-1969-11-15.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11493#sec3","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(1) the White House Office shall provide or arrange for support­\ning clerical, administrative, and other staff services for the Council,  \nand (2) each Federal department and agency which is represented on  \nthe Council shall furnish the Council such information Und other  \nassistance as may be available.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"34 FR 18289, PDF pages 5-6; Sec. 3(1)","sha256":"f522d7ceb7cb8dd8a14d4ceaad5eecedb213f066d2dd6b9e5fc36c9b76b4d445","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1969-11-15/pdf/FR-1969-11-15.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11493#sec3(1)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 4. Construction.  Nothing in this order shall be construed as  \nsubjecting any department, establishment, or other instrumentality of  \nthe executive branch of the Federal government or the head thereof,  \nor any function vested by law in or assigned pursuant to law to any  \nsuch agency or head, to the authority of any other such agency or head  \nor as abrogating, modifying, or restricting any such function in any  \nmanner.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"34 FR 18289, PDF pages 5-6; Sec. 4","sha256":"f522d7ceb7cb8dd8a14d4ceaad5eecedb213f066d2dd6b9e5fc36c9b76b4d445","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1969-11-15/pdf/FR-1969-11-15.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11493#sec4","state_at_cutoff":null}],"original_representation":{"page_or_item":"34 FR 18289, PDF pages 5-6","sha256":"f522d7ceb7cb8dd8a14d4ceaad5eecedb213f066d2dd6b9e5fc36c9b76b4d445","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1969-11-15/pdf/FR-1969-11-15.pdf"},"research_rationale":"","savings_residuals":null,"schema":"eo-lifecycle-claim/v1","unresolved_material_gaps":["DRAFT: state_at_cutoff not decided for 10 clause(s); clause inventory completeness not confirmed","DRAFT: whole-order ending not established","DRAFT: savings and residual effects not closed","DRAFT: later_source_search not recorded (machine searches are proposals only; paste them after judging them adequate and resolving every CONFLICT line)"],"whole_order_end":null,"whole_order_status":"no"},"draft_schema":"eo-claim-draft/v1","instrument_id":"EO:11493"}
